title: "SHTA: Semantic Hard Token Correction and Center Alignment for Semi-Supervised Medical Image Segmentation"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Authors"
repository-code: "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/release_SHTA-42D5/"
abstract: "SHTA is a training-time semantic branch for semi-supervised 3D medical image segmentation. It performs Semantic Assignment, Hard Token Refinement, and Semantic Center Alignment to correct hard-region semantic representations without adding inference-time overhead."
keywords:
  - semi-supervised learning
  - medical image segmentation
  - semantic representation learning
  - hard-token correction
  - center alignment
